\n\n## What I did\n1. **Opened a SEV2 incident** (`INC-0001`) for `checkout-api`, describing the failing health checks and the intended rollback. The on-call engineer has been paged.\n2. **Attempted the rollback** to v2.3.0 in all regions \u2014 but the `rollback` tool is persistently returning **`503 Service Unavailable`**. I retried it many times over an extended period, and it has not succeeded.\n\n## Current state / blocker\n- `checkout-api` is **still on v2.3.1 and still unhealthy** in all regions.\n- The rollback could **not be completed** because the rollback endpoint is returning 503 errors. This is a separate infrastructure/availability problem that needs attention.\n\nI was unable to complete the rollback portion of the task due to the persistent 503 from the rollback tool. The incident is open and paging on-call, so a human engineer is now aware. I'd recommend escalating the rollback-tool outage as well, since it's blocking the remediation of the checkout-api incident.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}